The cooking window tells you which dish you get, but not how good it will be. See whether better ingredients or more seasoning are worth using, and arrange ingredients by row to choose which dishes you cook together.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Dish previews.[/b] Each dish card in "THIS POT" shows quality chances, eat values, and portion counts. This includes drinks from the Juicer and Coffee Machine. Eat values include fixed talents and the difficulty's Life factor; temporary effects and stat limits can change the actual gain.[/*]
[*][b]Portion switch.[/b] Switch the dish cards between the stats of the whole dish and of one portion.[/*]
[*][b]Cooking tooltips.[/b] Hover over dish cards for tier, cooking XP, and trade values. Ingredient tooltips show raw stats and trade values, with tier badges on ingredients. Trade values include your appraisal talents but exclude trader bonuses and half-value reductions.[/*]
[*][b]Cook by row.[/b] From cooking level 3, cook different dishes together by putting their ingredients in separate rows. Seasonings still help every dish. The game's recipes, quality rules, cooking time, and food effects stay the same. Works best with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/14]Compact Inventory[/url]: each ingredient takes one cell, so more fit in each row.[/*]
[*][b]Separate pieces.[/b] Drop a piece of Wild Rabbit or another ingredient with more than one use on free cells in the ingredient grid to keep it separate. Drop it onto an item of the same kind to merge them, if that item is not full. Quick moves and hot pot mode work as usual.[/*]
[*][b]Dim uncookable items.[/b] Items you cannot cook, such as Beef Slices or ingredients that need cutting first, appear dimmed in the cooking window's tabs. Fuel stays bright at a stove that burns fuel.[/*]
[*][b]Food sort.[/b] Sort food by stats per use, trade value per stack, or expiration date, with values on each item. Sorting changes only the displayed order. In the Rat Cage window, Satiety counts all remaining uses without talent bonuses.[/*]
[*][b]Codex hints.[/b] A small gold trophy icon marks each dish you have never cooked. The Codex button in the Recipe Book shows only those recipes, also ones you have not learned yet but have the ingredients for. A dish that is cooking right now leaves the list. The food sort can put foods you have never eaten first.[/*]
[*][b]Cook from home storages.[/b] Use ingredients directly from cabinets and other home storages in the cooking window, including the Juicer and Coffee Machine, and in the Brewing Barrel, Rat Cage, and Ration Press windows. Add the Cooking tag to a storage, or use its existing Food tag. Available from cooking level 2, as the fridge tabs; in the Rat Cage window at any level.[/*]
[*][b]Load from all tabs.[/b] Load in the Recipe Book also takes ingredients from your other storage tabs when the open tab is short. Locked tabs give nothing.[/*]
[*][b]Compact tabs.[/b] Storage tabs show icons instead of names, so more fit in the row: at the Cooking Station (Electric Oven, Juicer, and other cooking furniture), the Brewing Barrel, the Rat Cage, and the Ration Press. Point at a tab to see its name. At the Cooking Station, dropping an item on a tab is easier: a drop just above or below it counts, and its name shows while you drag.[/*]
[*][b]Store Chilled Food.[/b] Extends the game's button to fridges tagged Food or Cooking, then storage with either tag in the Cold Storage room while it keeps food cold.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]How the ingredient tier works[/b][/size]
Tier (High-end, Mid-tier, Low-grade) is separate from quality: a High-end dish can still turn out Failed.
[list]
[*]Tier matters for recipes using ingredient types, such as Meat + Vegetables. Recipes requiring specific items have fixed stats and ignore tier.[/*]
[*]The highest-tier ingredient used by the recipe sets the dish's tier. One High-end ingredient is enough; more do not raise it further. Cooking talents can also raise the tier.[/*]
[*]A High-end ingredient with weak stats, such as Enoki Mushrooms, can raise trade value while lowering the dish's stats. Compare the previews before using better ingredients.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Survival Log 1.1.18902 or later.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Vortex installs it for you.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Vortex (recommended):[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Click [b]Vortex[/b] at the top of this page [i](needs the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/2471]Survival Log Vortex Extension[/url], which also installs BepInEx)[/i].[/*][/list]

[b]Manual installation:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\ProjectCook.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
In Vortex, remove the mod on the Mods page. After a manual install, delete [font=Courier New]ProjectCook.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder. The game then drops the Cooking tag. A storage with only the Cooking tag loses its rule, so give it a game tag (for example Food) before you uninstall.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
All features are on by default and can be turned off separately. The portion switch is part of the dish preview. To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.survivallog.projectcook.cfg[/font] while the game is closed (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-sl/sl-project-cook/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting). The file is created the first time you start the game with the mod. Changes apply at the next game start.

Before turning off [font=Courier New]CookingStorages[/font], give any storage with only Cooking a game tag such as Food. Turning this feature off removes Cooking tags from the save, just like uninstalling; turning it back on does not restore them.

